# Pinned dependency versions for CI and Docker builds.
# See engdocs/archive/designs/image-dependency-versioning.md for the versioning
# strategy (archived, but still the only written record of it).
#
# Update these when bumping automation/image pins. The internal/deps package
# defines minimum compatible versions (may lag behind these pins).

DOLT_VERSION=2.6.0
BD_REPO=Voxist/beads
# BD_VERSION is the bd binary CI and images run alongside gc — the VERSION
# STRING, matching what cmd/bd/version.go declares in the pinned source. It is
# asserted and stamped by contrib/k8s/Dockerfile.agent.
#
# FORK-FIRST BRIDGE (supersedes the ADR-0026 C5 upstream bridge; ga-zzcjs):
# the fleet's bd builds from the Voxist/beads fork, which carries schema
# 0074/0031 plus fork-only fixes; no published upstream release carries 0074
# yet (upstream v1.3.x, through v1.3.4, tops out at 0066; 0067-0074 are on
# upstream main only).
# BD_SOURCE_REF is the commit the fork's annotated v1.96.0 tag names
# (9dbe41b77, the Voxist/beads#79 merge -- `v1.96.0^{}` resolves to it;
# cmd/bd/version.go declares "1.96.0" there).
# It descends from 4ff2418f7 (v1.95.0, schema 0072/0028) along fork main
# through Voxist/beads#78, the resync that merges upstream main 3c205e0a4
# (= BD_LIB_REF below, 64 upstream commits past 43f41374a, including
# upstream's 1.3.3 security fixes) into fork main, and #79, the 1.96.0
# release. Its migrations beyond v1.95.0 are all upstream-authored and arrive
# through #78; #78 adds only prepared-dml-grandfather.txt entries under
# migrations/, so schema is 0074/0031 here, identical to upstream 3c205e0a4.
# bd 1.96.0 still requires Dolt >= 2.6.0 (DOLT_VERSION above).
#
# This pin moves the fleet from schema 0072/0028 to 0074/0031 (vp-pb00j).
# Main lane: 0073_add_arrival_seq (nullable arrival_seq on issues and wisps,
# unique index uk_wisps_arrival_seq) and 0074_create_id_tombstones (empty
# id_tombstones and clone-local wisp_id_tombstones tables). Ignored lane:
# 0029_add_wisps_arrival_seq and 0030_create_wisp_id_tombstones (the
# clone-local twins of 0073/0074) and 0031_restore_preflip_events (a marker
# whose pre-migration repair refills the clone-local events table from the
# clone's own history before the events-plane flip; no commit, no tracked
# write). The ignored lane is not gated on its own: it runs in the same
# `bd migrate schema` pass as the main lane, after it.
#
# DEPLOY GC FIRST. Deploy gc carrying this pin minutes (not hours) before the
# migration, in the same window. gc linked at 0074 sees a 0072 database as
# BEHIND: its preflight fails the native lane and gc falls back to the bd
# CLI (bd 1.95.0 still serves 0072), which is correct but slower. The
# reverse order is unsafe: gc linked at 0072 refuses a 0074 database
# (CheckForwardDrift -> SchemaSkewError), and a native store that reconnects
# after the migration hard-fails rather than falling back. bd 1.96.0 never
# migrates an existing database without consent (BD_ALLOW_MIGRATE,
# BD_ALLOW_REMOTE_MIGRATE or `bd migrate schema`), so after gc the swap is
# two steps: install bd 1.96.0, then run `bd migrate schema` once per
# database. beads.allow_schema_behind_migrate stays off.
#
# The schema 0069 -> 0072 move (ga-s69mk.18) was the previous pin's, and the
# 0067 -> 0069 move (ga-b2q0c) the one before; both merged before their
# controlled rollout window and were deployed only inside it.
#
# BEADS_DOLT_AUTO_START=0 remains load-bearing. What ga-rpgvw's fix proves is
# that the bd BINARY honours the workspace config key on the library-consumer
# auto-start path -- not that every rig is running a bd that carries the fix.
# This pin is not permission to drop the env var anywhere: remove it per rig
# only after `bd version` on that rig reports the fixed version (>= 1.92.0),
# never fleet-wide in one step. See ga-rpgvw.
#
# Three pins, three different things:
#
#   BD_SOURCE_REF  — the Voxist/beads commit the bd BINARY builds from
#                    (images via Dockerfile.agent, CI via
#                    install-bd-archive.sh with BD_REPO).
#   BD_LIB_REF     — the upstream commit gc's go.mod LINKS as a library.
#                    Fork commits do not resolve on the module path
#                    (github.com/steveyegge/beads redirects to the upstream
#                    repo), so the lib pin is an UPSTREAM commit the fork
#                    build descends from, with no fork-only deltas.
#                    Here that is 3c205e0a4 (vp-pb00j), the upstream
#                    gastownhall/beads main commit the Voxist/beads fork
#                    resyncs onto in Voxist/beads#78. It carries schema
#                    0074/0031: main 0073_add_arrival_seq and
#                    0074_create_id_tombstones, and ignored
#                    0029_add_wisps_arrival_seq,
#                    0030_create_wisp_id_tombstones and
#                    0031_restore_preflip_events. Its ignored-lane cursor
#                    reality gains a fourth floored sentinel table,
#                    wisp_id_tombstones at floor 29, which
#                    internal/beads/proxyendpoint mirrors.
#                    The bd binary pins above (v1.96.0, 9dbe41b77) descend
#                    from it and carry the same schema, so binary and
#                    library are in step.
#                    The previous lib pin was 43f41374a (schema 0072/0028),
#                    an ancestor of 3c205e0a4.
#                    go.mod's pseudo-version commit must equal this ref
#                    (enforced by TestBuildPinnedBDBinaryForTestsUsesGoModSource
#                    and scripts/bd_version_pin_test.go).
#   BD_SOURCE_SHA256 — sha256 of the BD_SOURCE_REF source tarball from BD_REPO
#                    (https://github.com/<BD_REPO>/archive/<BD_SOURCE_REF>.tar.gz,
#                    the file Dockerfile.agent verifies).
#
# When a release >= 0074 exists on a repo the module path resolves: set
# BD_VERSION to that tag, delete BD_SOURCE_REF/BD_LIB_REF/BD_SOURCE_SHA256,
# and repin go.mod — in ONE change.
BD_VERSION=v1.96.0
BD_SOURCE_REF=9dbe41b77dbfbce1bcde5d5326f0e9f69f27336f
BD_LIB_REF=3c205e0a41e42c01be5dd2c1df6bf870b6104482
BD_SOURCE_SHA256=50597482f556c2fccb9b969a84b04192b97d8fd481731e50327ed055e5f509fd
BR_VERSION=0.1.20

# Cross-version contract-test matrix pins.
# See engdocs/design/beads-gascity-contract-test-system.md.
# BD_PREV_VERSION is the minimum-supported bd: a published release whose tarball
# SHA is pinned in .github/scripts/install-bd-archive.sh (no API fallback on the
# required path). BD_CURRENT_VERSION is the bleeding-edge cell at BD_CURRENT_REF
# (a gastownhall/beads commit). Bump BD_CURRENT_REF deliberately, in lockstep
# with the vendored corpus, per the coordination protocol. The required cells
# run under Bazel against release archives (MODULE.bazel bd_bin_v*, kept on
# these pins by scripts/bd_contract_pins_test.go), so BD_CURRENT_REF must be
# BD_CURRENT_VERSION's tag commit; an untagged ref needs a source-built bd
# target first.
#
# The matrix axis is BD_PREV_VERSION vs BD_CURRENT_VERSION -- v1.3.0 against
# v1.3.4 -- and BD_VERSION is not a cell in it, so the installable default
# is free to sit anywhere at or above the floor without narrowing the axis.
# Upstream sits BD_VERSION on the current cell's own tag so its go.mod pin and
# the bd on PATH are the same beads. This fork does NOT: the fork-first bridge
# above deliberately splits them (BD_VERSION/BD_SOURCE_REF = Voxist fork build,
# BD_LIB_REF = go.mod's upstream ancestor), and scripts/bd_version_pin_test.go
# skips the unified-pin assertion while a bridge ref is set (ga-zzcjs).
# BD_CURRENT_REF moves with upstream's vendored corpus under
# internal/beads/testdata/corpus, which this resync took together with the bump.
#
# BD_PREV_VERSION is v1.3.0, the first tested bd release carrying the
# `--if-assignee`/`--if-status` conditional-release flags (beads#5008). bd
# v1.2.0/v1.2.1 had them but were accidental, untested releases, and v1.2.2
# re-released the v1.1.2 code without them. BdStore.ReleaseIfCurrent has no
# path without those flags, so a bd below the floor gets a typed
# ErrConditionalReleaseUnsupported. cmd/gc bdMinVersion restates this value
# (scripts/bd_version_pin_test.go).
BD_PREV_VERSION=v1.3.0
BD_CURRENT_VERSION=v1.3.4
BD_CURRENT_REF=7ef2fd05eb0cd3bdbde051f93cfc14ccf270cdde
